# Line endings are pinned, not inherited from the contributor's git config.
#
# This matters here for three concrete reasons:
#   * tests/snapshots/*.ast are compared byte-for-byte by parser_snapshots.rs,
#     so a CRLF checkout could fail otherwise-passing tests;
#   * tools/*.sh and kernel/build.sh are consumed by Linux shells;
#   * kernel/boot.S and bootasm.rs feed the assembler and include_str!.
#
# Default: normalise to LF in the repository and check out LF everywhere.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows-only tooling is conventionally CRLF.
*.ps1   text eol=crlf
*.bat   text eol=crlf
*.cmd   text eol=crlf

# Binaries: never convert.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.gif   binary
*.bin   binary
*.elf   binary
*.o     binary
*.a     binary
*.so    binary
*.wav   binary
*.zip   binary
*.gz    binary

# Diffs that humans actually want to read.
*.md    diff
*.rs    diff
*.HR    diff
